# Aliyun nginx → Volcengine minikb (kb.liuyidi.me)

Same pattern as mini-auth (`auth.liuyidi.me` → Tencent): DNS and TLS stay on
Aliyun; app traffic is reverse-proxied to Volcengine.

```text
https://kb.liuyidi.me  →  Aliyun nginx:443  →  http://101.96.224.232:80
```

(`MINIKB_PORT` on Volcengine maps host `:80` → container `:8080`.)

App publish: [`.github/workflows/publish-volcengine-minikb.yml`](../.github/workflows/publish-volcengine-minikb.yml)

## Install on Aliyun (TLS already issued for kb.liuyidi.me)

```nginx
upstream demo_kb { server 101.96.224.232:80; keepalive 8; }

server {
    listen 443 ssl http2;
    server_name kb.liuyidi.me;
    # ssl_certificate … (existing certbot paths)

    client_max_body_size 64m;

    location = / { return 302 /ui/; }

    location / {
        proxy_pass http://demo_kb;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto https;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Port 443;
        proxy_connect_timeout 10s;
        proxy_read_timeout 300s;
    }
}
```

## Volcengine firewall

Allow **Aliyun ECS** (`116.62.35.76`) to reach TCP **80** on Volcengine (currently open). Prefer locking SG to that IP rather than `0.0.0.0/0` if possible.

## Verify

```bash
curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1/health/live          # on Volcengine (host port 80)
curl -fsS https://kb.liuyidi.me/health          # via Aliyun
curl -fsS -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" https://kb.liuyidi.me/ui/
```
